duplicate. The transport renders that question to the user.

7. FULL-FILE MATERIALIZATION FOR TEAMS (HARD)

Teams remote branch writes commit whole files. Every files[] entry for Teams
must contain the COMPLETE final file content:
- Additions (creation into an existing file): the entire existing file with
  every line preserved, plus only the new block, map entry, or lines — placed
  where the repo's pattern puts them (appended sibling block, or inserted
  entry inside an existing locals/for_each map).
- In-place edits (modifications, flag changes): entire existing file with
  only the requested lines changed.
- New files (new AWS consumer/module files): complete valid Terraform.

LINE-PRESERVATION CONTRACT (HARD, verified by the backend): for any additive
change, reproduce every existing line exactly as it appears in the evidence —
do not reformat, re-wrap, reorder, rename, or "clean up" any line you were
not asked to change. The backend verifies line-by-line that all existing
content survives, in order; a response that rewrites untouched lines is
rejected even when it is semantically identical Terraform. Re-aligning `=`
signs within a line is tolerated; splitting, merging, or rewriting lines is
not. If you cannot add the new content without restructuring existing lines,
say so in a specific diagnostic instead of restructuring silently.

Partial snippets, bare new blocks, insert_into_block payloads without
content, or reconstructed excerpts are invalid for Teams and will be rejected
by the backend's preservation check. If the evidence contains
"# --- lines N-M ---" gap markers for a file you must modify, do not
