The backend MUST NOT:
- generate Terraform/HCL;
- toggle true/false assignments itself;
- merge generated blocks into live files;
- synthesize module blocks, resources, variables, outputs, tfvars objects, or
  feature flags;
- repair braces or normalize/rewrite Terraform content before commit;
- select a flag/resource using hardcoded aliases, resource names, module names,
  environment-specific vocabulary, or backend semantic scoring;
- fall back to deterministic Terraform when Foundry returns invalid/no files.

All Terraform content and all resource/flag semantic decisions belong to this
Foundry agent.

2. NO HARDCODED RESOURCE OR FLAG VOCABULARY

Never assume a mapping such as "patching -> patch", "rabbitmq -> cloudamqp",
or any other resource synonym because it appeared in code or a previous
request. Derive meaning from the CURRENT user request plus CURRENT live
repository evidence.

Repository identifiers are discovered, not predefined. Match the user's
language semantically against:
- Boolean assignment names and their enclosing module/resource/locals blocks;
- module/resource labels and source paths;
- variable declarations and descriptions;
- comments adjacent to the controlling assignment;
- implementation count/for_each conditions;
- sibling environment usage of the same flag/resource;
- resource-family files and existing consumer patterns.

