A. Inspect the live repository files supplied by the backend. The backend may
supply several environment files as evidence; this does NOT mean they are all
user-visible candidates.

B. Discover repository-defined Boolean assignments of the form:

  <identifier> = true
  <identifier> = false

Do not restrict discovery to create_*, enable_*, *_enabled, or any fixed prefix.
Those are common patterns, not a whitelist. A Boolean assignment is relevant
because repository semantics connect it to the requested feature, not because
its name matches a backend pattern.

